* Week 8: the four non-retrying primitives, plus LEN, exercised against
* a subject that makes their differences visible (research/snobol/
* 03-pattern-matching.md, "The primitive patterns"). BREAK's null-match
* case is the one this session flags explicitly: run with --trace to see
* it succeed having consumed nothing, right where the digits begin.
        SUBJECT = 'HELLO123'
        SUBJECT LEN(5)                 :F(FAIL1)
        OUTPUT = 'LEN OK'
FAIL1   SUBJECT ANY('XYZ')             :F(ANYOK)
        OUTPUT = 'ANY SHOULD HAVE FAILED'      :(SKIP1)
ANYOK   OUTPUT = 'ANY CORRECTLY FAILED'
SKIP1   SUBJECT NOTANY('XYZ')          :F(FAIL2)
        OUTPUT = 'NOTANY OK'
FAIL2   SUBJECT SPAN('HELO')           :F(FAIL3)
        OUTPUT = 'SPAN OK'
FAIL3   DIGITS = '123ABC'
        DIGITS BREAK('ABC')            :F(FAIL4)
        OUTPUT = 'BREAK OK'
FAIL4   ALREADYDIGIT = 'ABC'
        ALREADYDIGIT BREAK('ABC')      :F(NULLFAIL)
        OUTPUT = 'BREAK NULL-MATCH OK'         :(STOP)
NULLFAIL        OUTPUT = 'BREAK NULL-MATCH SHOULD HAVE SUCCEEDED'
STOP    N = N
